  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Veterans Affairs spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $70B in contracts in FY2026 to date. The VA recorded 59,844 awards with an average award size of $1.2M, and obligations fell 10.6% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Veterans Affairs buy?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs buys health care, pharmaceuticals, physician services, IT, construction, and medical supplies. The top NAICS categories in FY2026 to date are Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers at $29.4B, Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing at $11.1B, Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) at $7.6B, Computer Systems Design Services at $3.4B, and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $2.5B, with other categories including Other Computer Related Services at $2.1B and Medical, Dental, and Hospital Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers at $913M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Veterans Affairs's largest contractors?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs's largest contractors by obligations are OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC., MCKESSON CORPORATION, and TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP. OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. received $19.9B, MCKESSON CORPORATION received $10.8B, and TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP received $9.8B, followed by QTC MEDICAL SERVICES INC at $2.2B and OPTUMSERVE HEALTH SERVICES, INC. at $1.8B."
